{"kind":"panel","id":"89a55b99-bd1c-4249-9cae-c38492fa8ac1","type":"59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c","name":"Panel","nick":"Deconstruct anything","desc":"A panel for custom notes and text values","box":[300,60,900,170],"src":[],"text":"Deconstruct anything - look inside any object of Alpaca4d.\n\nDeconstruct takes an object of Alpaca4d - an element, a section, a material, a load, a model, a result - and gives each of its fields and properties an output of its own, named after it. The first, Object Class, says what the object is.\n\nHere a cantilever, an IPE 300 of S355 4 m long, built in and loaded at its tip, is opened up piece by piece: the beam, then the section it carries, then the section's material, each Deconstruct fed from the one before; the point load; and the assembled model, then every node in it - one Deconstruct takes a list of the same kind of object too.\n\nUse it to check what reached a component, to read a number Alpaca4d keeps but shows nowhere else, or to pick objects out for filters and views of your own. Plug something else into any of them: its outputs change to fit, once it is solved.","colour":[255,255,250,90]}
],
